{"created": "2020-09-15T04:58:09.066336+00:00", "modified": "2021-12-19T04:10:53.292875+00:00", "id": 4010759, "conceptrecid": "4010758", "doi": "10.1145/3394171.3413528", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.1145/3394171.3413528", "metadata": {"title": "INCLUDE: A Large Scale Dataset for Indian Sign Language Recognition", "doi": "10.1145/3394171.3413528", "publication_date": "2020-10-16", "description": "<p><strong>Dataset Details</strong>: The INCLUDE dataset has 4292 videos (the paper mentions 4287 videos but 5 videos were added later). The videos used for training are mentioned in train.csv (3475), while that used for testing is mentioned in test.csv (817 files). Each video is a recording of 1 ISL sign, signed by deaf students from St. Louis School for the Deaf, Adyar, Chennai.</p>\n\n<p>INCLUDE50 has 766 train videos and 192 test videos.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Train-Test Split:</strong> Please download the train-test split for&nbsp;INCLUDE and INCLUDE50 from here:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tGjOR9xbk279ZUYnmk3BE-ktcWBdS24w/view?usp=sharing\">Train-Test Split</a></p>\n\n<p><strong>Publication Link</strong><em>:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3394171.3413528\">https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3394171.3413528</a></em></p>\n\n<p><strong>AI4Bharat website</strong><em>: <a href=\"https://ai4bharat.org/include-dataset\">https://sign-language.ai4bharat.org/</a></em></p>\n\n<p><strong>Download Instructions</strong></p>\n\n<p>For ease of access, we have prepared a Shell Script to download all the parts of the dataset and extract them to form the complete INCLUDE dataset.</p>\n\n<p><em>You can find the script here:&nbsp;<a href=\"http://bit.ly/include_dl\">http://bit.ly/include_dl</a></em></p>\n\n<p><strong>Paper Abstract:</strong> <em>Indian Sign Language (ISL) is a complete language with its own grammar, syntax, vocabulary and several unique linguistic attributes. It is used by over 5 million deaf people in India. Currently, there is no publicly available dataset on ISL to evaluate Sign Language Recognition (SLR) approaches. In this work, we present the Indian Lexicon Sign Language Dataset - INCLUDE - an ISL dataset that contains 0.27 million frames across 4,287 videos over 263 word signs from 15 different word categories. INCLUDE is recorded with the help of experienced signers to provide close resemblance to natural conditions. A subset of 50 word signs is chosen across word categories to define INCLUDE-50 for rapid evaluation of SLR methods with hyperparameter tuning. The best performing model achieves an accuracy of 94.5% on the INCLUDE-50 dataset and 85.6% on the INCLUDE dataset</em></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Sridhar, Advaith", "affiliation": "IIT Madras, AI4Bharat"}, {"name": "Ganesan, Rohith Gandhi", "affiliation": "IIT Madras, AI4Bharat"}, {"name": "Kumar, Pratyush", "affiliation": "IIT Madras, AI4Bharat"}, {"name": "Khapra, Mitesh", "affiliation": "IIT Madras, AI4Bharat"}], "keywords": ["Indian Sign Language", "ISL", "NLP", "Dataset", "INCLUDE", "INCLUDE-50"], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "meeting": {"title": "ACM Multimedia 2020", "acronym": "ACMMM2020", "dates": "12-16 October 2020", "url": "https://2020.acmmm.org/"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "4010758"}}]}, "notes": "Please use the train-test split mentioned in the description"}, "title": "INCLUDE: A Large Scale Dataset for Indian Sign Language Recognition", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4010759", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4010759", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4010759?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1145/3394171.3413528", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.1145/3394171.3413528", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.1145/3394171.3413528", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4010759/draft/pids/doi"